{"id":"r8","level":1,"levelName":"Reading","n":8,"of":8,"title":"The dot that changes the sound","titleHe":"דָּגֵשׁ","goal":"Read בּ/ב, כּ/כ, פּ/פ — and sound out whole words unaided.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"A dot inside a letter is a dagesh. In modern Hebrew it changes the sound of exactly three letters."},{"type":"dagesh","items":[{"soft":"בֿ","hard":"בּ","en":"vet → bet","sound":"v becomes b"},{"soft":"כֿ","hard":"כּ","en":"khaf → kaf","sound":"kh becomes k"},{"soft":"פֿ","hard":"פּ","en":"fe → pe","sound":"f becomes p"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"The other nineteen letters take a dagesh too, but it makes no audible difference today — so when you see one elsewhere, read straight through it."},{"type":"text","body":"That is the whole reading system. Everything from here is words and grammar; you can now sound out anything that carries vowel marks."}],"vocab":[{"he":"בַּיִת","en":"house","translit":"bayit"},{"he":"כֶּלֶב","en":"dog","translit":"kelev"},{"he":"פַּעַם","en":"once, a time","translit":"pa'am"},{"he":"אוֹכֵל","en":"eats","translit":"ochel"},{"he":"סַבָּא","en":"grandfather","translit":"saba"},{"he":"מִשְׁפָּחָה","en":"family","translit":"mishpacha"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"בּ — with the dot — sounds like?","options":["k","b","p","ch as in Bach"],"correct":1,"prompt":"בּ"},{"type":"choice","q":"כּ — with the dot — sounds like?","options":["b","ch as in Bach","k","p"],"correct":2,"prompt":"כּ"},{"type":"choice","q":"פּ — with the dot — sounds like?","options":["b","p","k","ch as in Bach"],"correct":1,"prompt":"פּ"},{"type":"choice","q":"Where is the dot in shin?","options":["under the letter","dot on the left","there is no dot","dot on the right"],"correct":3,"prompt":"שׁ"},{"type":"choice","q":"Where is the dot in sin?","options":["there is no dot","dot on the left","under the letter","dot on the right"],"correct":1,"prompt":"שׂ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["city","house","yesterday","that, which (literary)"],"correct":1,"prompt":"בַּיִת","translit":"bayit"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["they (archaic)","in, at","dog","nevertheless"],"correct":2,"prompt":"כֶּלֶב","translit":"kelev"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “house”?","options":["פֶּה","לוֹ","בַּיִת","שְׁנַיִם"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “eats”?","options":["יֵשׁ","קוֹנֶה","נִגְמַר","אוֹכֵל"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"פַּעַם","translit":"pa'am","en":"once, a time"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["כֶּלֶב","dog"],["פַּעַם","once, a time"],["מִשְׁפָּחָה","family"],["בַּיִת","house"],["אוֹכֵל","eats"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “family”?","options":["מִשְׁפָּחָה","עֵץ","שָׁר","אוֹכֵל"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “once, a time”?","options":["פַּעַם","שֹׁרֶשׁ","מְקֻבָּל","סֵפֶר"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["מִשְׁפָּחָה","פַּעַם","בַּיִת","כֶּלֶב"],"correct":1,"say":"פַּעַם","he":true},{"type":"read","he":"סַבָּא","translit":"saba","en":"grandfather"},{"type":"read","he":"מִשְׁפָּחָה","translit":"mishpacha","en":"family"}]}